{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-105748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-105748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =2(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-2) & =2({x}^{2}-4x+4)({x}^{2}-4x+4) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}+16{x}^{2}-16x+4{x}^{2}-16x+16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-32x+16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-105748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-105748" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-105748" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{4}+10{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}+64x+16"] ["math" "2{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}+64x+32"] ["math" "2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-64x+16"] ["math" "2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32"] ["math" "2{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-64x+32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-105748" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-107795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,{x}_{2}=2,{x}_{3}=-4$ and ${x}_{4}=4$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-107795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,{x}_{2}=2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-1)(x-2)(x-(-4))(x-4) \\\\  & =(x-1)(x-2)(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x-2)(x+4)(x-4) & =({x}^{2}-3x+2)({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-16{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}+48x+2{x}^{2}-32 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-107795" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-107795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-107795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+12x"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}+24x-32"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+6x-32"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+8x-32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-107795" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $9.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,576$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =9(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-(-4))(x-4) \\\\  & =9(x+2)(x+2)(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+2)(x+2)(x+4)(x-4) & =9({x}^{2}+4x+4)({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & =9({x}^{4}-16{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-64x+4{x}^{2}-64) \\\\  & =9({x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-64x-64) \\\\  & =9{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-108{x}^{2}-576x-576.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=9{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-108{x}^{2}-576x-576.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-319949" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319949" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9x^4+36x^3-108x^2-576x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and ${x}_{4}=5$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,40$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and ${x}_{4}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x+2)(x+2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x+2)(x+2)(x-5) & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)({x}^{2}-3x-10) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-40x+4{x}^{2}-12x-40 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-52x-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-52x-40.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-319369" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319369" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^4+x^3-18x^2-52x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-1,$ and ${x}_{4}=3$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,6$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-1,$ and ${x}_{4}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)({x}^{2}-2x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6x+{x}^{2}-2x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-0{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-8x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-16x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-16x-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-319377" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-319377" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x^4-12x^2-16x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/07724ed5ffd4843ab0a23b0029eeec6291ae698aba71f56f99fb7ac565287932.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-(-1))(x-4)(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =1(x+1)(x-4)(x+2\\text{i})(x-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4)(x+2\\text{i})(x-2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-4x-4)({x}^{2}+(2\\text{i}-2\\text{i})x-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-3x-4)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}-12x-4{x}^{2}-16 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-8210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}-2x-16"] ["math" "{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+2x-8"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}-2x-8"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/fb8d76e5fb2e83676fbab4178b523bf8cbff076490f12fa8be17c37ce06e1820.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,100$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-2)(x-(-2))(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x-2x-4)({x}^{2}+5\\text{i}x-5\\text{i}x-(5\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4)({x}^{2}+25) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+25{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-100 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-320074" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320074" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^4+21x^2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/4eafeae1c77e3e75cb2b281181346eeb7e96ca5e1bd15ec11d722109469557a1.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,24$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2\\text{i}$  and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+2\\text{i}x-2\\text{i}x-(2\\text{i})^{2})({x}^{2}-x(1-\\text{i})-x(1+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-2x+2) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}-8x+8) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-8x+8) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24\\,.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-320292" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-320292" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^4-6x^3+18x^2-24x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-275317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/431ba020bfc39615e1d49a866c6ee7c30cf8cc8f84ebde6866ef0e0cb9c8708b.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,81$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-275317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{1}=1,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-3))(x-1)(x-(-3\\text{i}))(x-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x-1)(x+3\\text{i})(x-3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-1)(x+3\\text{i})(x-3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-x+3x-3)({x}^{2}-3\\text{i}x+3\\text{i}x-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+2x-3)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+9{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}+18x-3{x}^{2}-27) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+18x-27) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}+54x-81 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}+54x\\,-81.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-275317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-275317" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-275317" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x^4+6x^3+18x^2+54x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/8fb9e432fe79c363a42d362ef5c352eab6e8b55b83583f2a946ed9251ce293e3.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 1,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-1)(x-(-1))(x-(4\\text{i}))(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =1(x-1)(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-x-{1}^{2})({x}^{2}+4\\text{i}x-4\\text{i}x-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-1)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+16{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c22c077ae6e37e290c8eb396fba924c36b3cdc6597d1c4e1abb6c4c90d5d99b"} {"question" "q-8212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}+7x-4"] ["math" "{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16"] ["math" "{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+16"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+18"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "q-8212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/state.json" "file_sha256" "f50c059e0f2692d20a906a565bf50333879f0a2403f34c09b9b5e3dfee67b3e0"} {"question" "e-8801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=0, x_2=-1,x_3=2$ and $x_4=-3,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $4.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/example-8801.json" "file_sha256" "fbf62ebfe215f75dd30bc6d602cade5b03ef93cde3c6f0aa61780dde7bc06c55"} {"question" "e-8801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x_1=0, x_2=-1},$ ${x_3=2},$ and ${x_4=-3},$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=4},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =4(x-0)(x-(-1))(x-2)(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x+1)(x-2)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-0)(x+1)(x-2)(x+3) & =4({x}^{2}+x)({x}^{2}+x-6) \\\\  & =4({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-6x) \\\\  & =4({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-6x) \\\\  & =4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-24x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 4x^4+8x^3-20x^2-24x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/example-8801.json" "file_sha256" "fbf62ebfe215f75dd30bc6d602cade5b03ef93cde3c6f0aa61780dde7bc06c55"} {"question" "e-5796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/658fa5a494ef01b5924847335ce863aa8c6b5f8adee5ee97967a8c8bebd83a80.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/example-5796.json" "file_sha256" "bdf925dcce543f12596accafb893fa46c3a89d1f6a11d66a6b09b1e37bbb60f2"} {"question" "e-5796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x_1=-2},$ ${x_2=3},$ and ${x_{3,4}=1 \\pm 3\\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=1}.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (x-(-2))(x-(3))(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x-3)(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x-3)(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-3x+2x-6)({x}^{2}-x(1-3\\text{i})-x(1+3\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-x-6)({x}^{2}-2x+10) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-10x-6{x}^{2}+12x-60 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+2x-60 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 6x^2 + 2x - 60.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/example-5796.json" "file_sha256" "bdf925dcce543f12596accafb893fa46c3a89d1f6a11d66a6b09b1e37bbb60f2"}] "usage" {"e-8801" [] "q-8210" [] "e-5796" []} "basis" 2196 "retractions" [[17592186088345 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/897/Source/Images/q-8210.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1$."] [17592186087587 :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=0, x_2=-1,x_3=2$ and $x_4=-3$, and the coefficient of the quartic term is $4$. Find $P(x)$."] [17592186087587 :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{x_1=0, x_2=-1}\n$$\n\n${x_3=2}$, and ${x_4=-3}$, and the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=4}$, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3})(x - x_{4}) &= 4(x - 0)(x - (-1))(x - 2)(x - (-3)) \\\\\n&= 4(x - 0)(x + 1)(x - 2)(x + 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4(x - 0)(x + 1)(x - 2)(x + 3) &= 4(x^{2} + x)(x^{2} + x - 6) \\\\\n&= 4(x^{4} + x^{3} - 6x^{2} + x^{3} + x^{2} - 6x) \\\\\n&= 4(x^{4} + 2x^{3} - 5x^{2} - 6x) \\\\\n&= 4x^{4} + 8x^{3} - 20x^{2} - 24x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 4x^4+8x^3-20x^2-24x\n$$"] [17592186087512 :question/problem "The Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/897/Source/Images/0dcad03e8bddad5bbf3557260060a9c4.png)"] [17592186087512 :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x_1=-2}$, ${x_2=3}$, and\n\n$$\n{x_{3,4}=1 \\pm 3\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=1}$. Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= a(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3})(x - x_{4}) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (x - (-2))(x - (3))(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= (x + 2)(x - 3)(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 2)(x - 3)(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x^{2} - 3x + 2x - 6)(x^{2} - x(1 - 3\\textrm{i}) - x(1 + 3\\textrm{i}) + (1 + 3\\textrm{i})(1 - 3\\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x^{2} - x - 6)(x^{2} - 2x + 10) &=  \\\\\nx^{4} - 2x^{3} + 10x^{2} - x^{3} + 2x^{2} - 10x - 6x^{2} + 12x - 60 &=  \\\\\n&= x^{4} - 3x^{3} + 6x^{2} + 2x - 60 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 6x^2 + 2x - 60\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186087001 17592186087002 17592186087003 17592186087004 17592186087005] "immutable_fields" [[17592186087000 :answer-field/correct] [17592186087000 :answer-field/id] [17592186087000 :answer-field/key] [17592186087000 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
